      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({compose_project=\"ragweld\", compose_service=\"litellm\"} |~ \"Failed to export (span )?batch|Exception while exporting Span batch\" [$__range])) or (0 * sum(count_over_time({compose_project=\"ragweld\", compose_service=\"litellm\"} [$__range])))",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Observed native OTLP terminal export-error log lines, counted by batch rather than generation. Retry warnings are excluded. Zero means scoped gateway logs were available with no matching terminal errors in the same range; it does not prove delivery. No scoped gateway logs remains unavailable. Unlogged failures are not measured. Provider request failures are not callback-delivery failures."
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "content": "## Spend and token coverage\nThe default selected range is midnight UTC to now: calendar-day totals, not a rolling 24 hours. Today (UTC) restores that range. Custom and absolute history selections keep their actual boundaries; rolling seven-day panels end at the selected end time.\n\nNative LiteLLM counters are scraped into Mimir. Increase/rate handle resets before aggregation and extrapolate between scrapes, so these are approximate gateway totals, not the exact run billing ledger. Missing or insufficient samples show No data, not zero. A recorded zero remains zero. Input and output make up total tokens; cached and reasoning subsets are not added again.\n\nLane labels begin when native telemetry is enabled. Older series and callers without lane metadata remain unattributed. Only calls actually routed through the gateway contribute; direct provider or local work remains outside this measurement. No run/corpus Prometheus labels or unsupported filters are used. Exact-run reconciliation and unmeasured components remain available in the run accounting API/UI.\n\nThe exporter panel counts native terminal OTLP error log lines from LiteLLM through the existing Loki pipeline. It is a batch diagnostic, not a generation-loss ledger or proof of successful Langfuse delivery. A zero is shown only when scoped gateway logs exist in the same range with no terminal errors. No scoped logs remains unavailable; zero does not prove delivery. Temporary retries that recover are excluded. Pinned LiteLLM proxy request-failure counters lack lane metadata and are not used as callback-delivery signals.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Operator Notes",
      "type": "text"
    }
